{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional.invariantForm_proportional_of_commutantScalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional.invariantForm_proportional_of_commutantScalar","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchurInvariantFormProportional.lean#L92-L107","doc":"**Schur proportionality of invariant forms.** If the commutant of `ρ` is scalar\n(the absolute-irreducibility hypothesis — every matrix commuting with all `ρ s` is\n`c • 1`), and `G₁` is a unit, then any invariant form `G₂` is a scalar multiple of\n`G₁`. This is the Option-B core: two invariant symmetric forms on an irreducible\nrepresentation are proportional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional.commute_of_invariantForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional.commute_of_invariantForm","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchurInvariantFormProportional.lean#L52-L90","doc":"**Key commuting step.** If `G₁` and `G₂` are both invariant forms for a\nrepresentation `ρ` by units, then `A = G₁⁻¹ * G₂` commutes with every `ρ s`. (This is\nwhy an invariant form defines a `ρ`-equivariant map to the dual.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional.InvariantForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.SchurInvariantFormProportional.InvariantForm","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/SchurInvariantFormProportional.lean#L47-L50","doc":"Invariance of a bilinear-form matrix `M` under `ρ s`: the transpose-sandwich\n`(ρ s)ᵀ * M * (ρ s) = M`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}